<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Nagar</h1><p class="st-meta">2600 BCE – 2200 BCE (approx.) · capital Nagar</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Nagar, a major city of the northern Syrian plains at Tell Brak, famed in the 3rd millennium BCE for breeding prized draught equids and later seized by Akkad.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Tell <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brak">Brak</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khabur-river">Khabur</a> basin had been one of the largest settlements of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> since the 4th millennium BCE. By c. 2600 BCE it was the centre of a kingdom called Nagar, which appears in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ebla">Ebla</a> archives as a regional power on the route between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ebla">Ebla</a> texts show Nagar exchanging gifts, envoys and royal marriages with its western neighbour, and supplying expensive kunga, hybrid draught animals bred from donkeys and wild asses, used to pull royal vehicles. Little is known of its internal government, since few texts have been found at the site itself.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 2300 BCE the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a> took control; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naram-sin">Naram-Sin</a> built a massive fortified storehouse at Tell <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brak">Brak</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkad">Akkad's</a> collapse a Hurrian kingdom called Nawar ruled from the city, and Tell Brak stayed occupied into the 2nd millennium BCE.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/nagar.jpg" alt="Nagar" width="320" height="172"><figcaption>Image: Zoeperkoe · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tell_Brak_001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>2600 BCE – 2200 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/27th-century-bce">27th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/23rd-century-bce">23rd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Nagar</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ancient Mesopotamian religion</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tell Brak, Nawar</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-2400&amp;focus=nagar" aria-label="Nagar on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5711 856 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Nagar lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6031 1112L6129 1232"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6129 1232h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6031 1112h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6031 1112h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=-2400&amp;focus=nagar">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

